 "equipment_type": "Chilled water ceiling cassette (fan coil) controller",
 "applies_to": "Modine SCW and CCW ductless chilled water ceiling cassettes, model digit 7 = C, with the factory microprocessor controller.",
 "summary": "The cassette's controller has an RS-485 port that talks native BACnet MS/TP (or Modbus RTU, chosen with DIP switch SW3.8). From the BMS you can switch the unit on and off, set mode, fan speed and cooling and heating setpoints, drive occupancy and lock out the local remote or touchscreen. Every tuning parameter (PID gains, fan delays, valve bands, fan speed percentages, freeze protection) is also exposed, along with the sensors, the valve and fan outputs and the relay outputs.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet MS/TP"
 ],
 "firmware": null,
 "default_device_instance": "315000 + MAC address (DIP switches SW1.1-SW1.6)",
 "access_inferred": false,
 "notes": [
  "The manual marks the sensor inputs and the analog and binary outputs as R/W; they are shown as printed.",
  "Ranges and defaults are printed in °F with °C in brackets; BV 2 C_F_Scale switches the display scale.",
  "Instances are not contiguous (e.g. AV 16, AV 25-26, BO 4 are not listed); only the printed objects are shown.",
  "ModeEffective value 5 ('None mode') applies to 2-pipe units; DI3 mode selection in 2-pipe needs BV 48 = 1.",
  "Source table: Table 9.1 BACnet Points List, manual pages 9-11 (105 objects)."
 ],
